WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:05.040
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie and this week
Game Of Thrones did some very unexpected but

00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:06.040
very big things.

00:00:06.040 --> 00:00:09.450
Bran came back into the story in a big way
and it seems like they’re changing some

00:00:09.450 --> 00:00:14.570
of the plot in the north so that the larger
story this season is a little more concise

00:00:14.570 --> 00:00:18.320
without dropping secondary characters as much
as it did last year.

00:00:18.320 --> 00:00:22.090
In addition, round 4 of the giveaway starts
now.

00:00:22.090 --> 00:00:26.210
If you’re finding me for the first time
just as a way to say thank you to all you

00:00:26.210 --> 00:00:28.189
guys for being so awesome I’m selecting
one random subscriber from the comments to

00:00:28.189 --> 00:00:29.690
give a $20 amazon gift card too.

00:00:29.690 --> 00:00:33.260
All you have to do to participate is be a
subscriber and leave a comment.

00:00:33.260 --> 00:00:35.219
I’ll announce the winner in my Q&amp;A video
tomorrow night.

00:00:35.219 --> 00:00:39.790
I was so happy with everything that happened
this week, let’s start with WTF moments

00:00:39.790 --> 00:00:41.079
and then I’ll do my review.

00:00:41.079 --> 00:00:44.160
Careful for Spoilers if you haven’t seen
the episode yet.

00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:47.469
Number 5 - Littlefinger explains the Purple
Wedding

00:00:47.469 --> 00:00:51.260
We have to give Sansa some credit, she figured
out most of what happened.

00:00:51.260 --> 00:00:55.489
But Littlefinger continues to creep the hell
out of us in the best possible way.

00:00:55.489 --> 00:00:57.800
He wants everything, but what does that even
mean.

00:00:57.800 --> 00:00:59.700
Does he want to sit on the Iron Throne?

00:00:59.700 --> 00:01:02.290
Or does he just want power over everyone.

00:01:02.290 --> 00:01:04.930
It think he just wants to be a god on earth.

00:01:04.930 --> 00:01:07.640
Just have the entire world serve his whims.

00:01:07.640 --> 00:01:10.060
Like you would think of characters in a tabletop
game.

00:01:10.060 --> 00:01:13.650
I think he just enjoys playing the game so
to speak.

00:01:13.650 --> 00:01:19.040
As opposed to Varys who actually seemed like
he had a noble purpose in mind, despite being

00:01:19.040 --> 00:01:20.189
pretty awful himself.

00:01:20.189 --> 00:01:24.880
Other big takeaways from this, they’re heading
to the Eyrie, Littlefinger is marrying Sansa’s

00:01:24.880 --> 00:01:28.170
crazy aunt and she’s just going to chill
out with them.

00:01:28.170 --> 00:01:31.880
And probably try to avoid Littlefinger in
the hallways.

00:01:31.880 --> 00:01:33.750
Number 4 - Daenerys takes Meereen

00:01:33.750 --> 00:01:39.140
It’s not really a seige so much as an infiltration,
but this was really similar to the way it

00:01:39.140 --> 00:01:40.140
happened in the books.

00:01:40.140 --> 00:01:44.689
There was never a big battle, Daenerys was
let in by the slaves after they turned on

00:01:44.689 --> 00:01:45.770
their masters.

00:01:45.770 --> 00:01:47.850
And her family just doubled in size.

00:01:47.850 --> 00:01:54.390
Remember, Meereen is as big as Astapor and
Yunkai combined.

00:01:54.390 --> 00:01:58.680
I loved Grey Worm in this episode, it was
like they let Daario be a badass last week,

00:01:58.680 --> 00:02:01.540
so now it was Grey Worm’s turn to have his
hero moment.

00:02:01.540 --> 00:02:05.560
I love how brainwashed he is, he doesn’t
care about returning to his home on the summer

00:02:05.560 --> 00:02:08.229
aisles, he just wants to kill the masters.

00:02:08.229 --> 00:02:13.970
Daenerys nailing them up was pretty hardcore,
but I like how much she craves the idea of

00:02:13.970 --> 00:02:14.970
justice and revengee.

00:02:14.970 --> 00:02:16.680
It really did feel more like revenge when
you saw that look on her face.

00:02:16.680 --> 00:02:20.620
Hands down though, my favorite part was the
big shot of the city that opens up to reveal

00:02:20.620 --> 00:02:23.140
the Targaryen flag on top of the pyramid.

00:02:23.140 --> 00:02:30.680
It’s like she’s slowly reclaiming the
honor and glory of house Targaryen.

00:02:30.680 --> 00:02:33.480
Number 3 - Burn Gorman Is the True King Of
The North

00:02:33.480 --> 00:02:37.060
I feel like Burn Gorman really won this episode
as an actor.

00:02:37.060 --> 00:02:41.250
Did anyone else get a Shakespeare Hamlet vibe
when he was talking to the skull.

00:02:41.250 --> 00:02:48.790
I flipped a little when they revealed it was
Lord Mormont’s skull.

00:02:48.790 --> 00:02:51.099
This was one of the huge changes from the
books.

00:02:51.099 --> 00:02:56.220
Burn Gorman’s character Karl is in the book,
but the show is doing something different

00:02:56.220 --> 00:02:57.280
with the Craster storyline.

00:02:57.280 --> 00:03:01.330
Personally I don’t mind, because it gives
them the opportunity to bring Bran back into

00:03:01.330 --> 00:03:06.080
the story in a big way and I know a lot of
you guys were saying you thought that was

00:03:06.080 --> 00:03:07.629
the weakest part of the plot so far.

00:03:07.629 --> 00:03:08.629
Bran just wasn’t really integral to the
story.

00:03:08.629 --> 00:03:13.580
I actually thought that Bran was going to
warg into Burn Gorman and make him kill himself.

00:03:13.580 --> 00:03:17.860
Because this isn’t in the books I’m wondering
if they’re going to actually do something

00:03:17.860 --> 00:03:18.860
like that.

00:03:18.860 --> 00:03:20.099
Or if Jon will make it there and rescue them.

00:03:20.099 --> 00:03:22.629
Number 2 - Jaime Gives Brienne Oathkeeper

00:03:22.629 --> 00:03:27.750
This was one of the big moments in the books
and I love the small changes they made on

00:03:27.750 --> 00:03:28.760
the show.

00:03:28.760 --> 00:03:34.489
In the books, the implied ‘ship between
Jaime and Brienne isn’t really as explicit

00:03:34.489 --> 00:03:35.489
as it is on the show.

00:03:35.489 --> 00:03:40.739
And you didn’t get to visually see the emotion
exploding all over Brienne’s face when Jaime

00:03:40.739 --> 00:03:42.110
gives her the sword and the armor.

00:03:42.110 --> 00:03:46.330
It’s almost like she’s so overcome with
feels that all she can think of is honor and

00:03:46.330 --> 00:03:47.330
duty.

00:03:47.330 --> 00:03:50.510
I wouldn’t mind if HBO just wanted to spin
off a show about the two of them.

00:03:50.510 --> 00:03:52.040
I could watch their scenes all day.

00:03:52.040 --> 00:03:54.459
That Podrick reveal was so much fun too.

00:03:54.459 --> 00:03:58.790
Just a perfect way to cut that intense scene
with comedy.

00:03:58.790 --> 00:04:03.540
In the books Podrick also travels with her,
but instead of Tyrion and Jaime sending him

00:04:03.540 --> 00:04:08.129
with her officially, he just kind of stalked
her from a distance until she accepted his

00:04:08.129 --> 00:04:12.780
assistance.

00:04:12.780 --> 00:04:21.660
And my Number 1 WTF Moment - The Court of
the White Walkers

00:04:21.660 --> 00:04:25.610
All I could think about as the white walker
rode into that landscape was of the Witch

00:04:25.610 --> 00:04:27.780
King’s castle from Lord of The Rings.

00:04:27.780 --> 00:04:30.900
It looked like the Superman’s Fortress of
Solitude if it were designed by the Witch

00:04:30.900 --> 00:04:32.380
King of Angmar.

00:04:32.380 --> 00:04:36.889
I saw a lot of people complaining on twitter
that this was a Winds of Winter Spoiler.

00:04:36.889 --> 00:04:41.430
I don’t know if that’s true, but it’s
kind of implied that we’re going to see

00:04:41.430 --> 00:04:45.180
a lot more white walker centric stuff then.

00:04:45.180 --> 00:04:47.890
Because it’s the next to last book.

00:04:47.890 --> 00:04:50.960
The white walker that actually performed the
transformation on that baby looked like it

00:04:50.960 --> 00:04:53.229
was a white walker that just held more rank
than the one that brought the baby.

00:04:53.229 --> 00:04:55.810
It kind of looked like he had a crown on his
head but I couldn’t tell.

00:04:55.810 --> 00:04:59.090
As if they have their own hierarchy.

00:04:59.090 --> 00:05:02.750
They perform their own kinds of necromancy
and magic.

00:05:02.750 --> 00:05:07.389
But the books haven’t really explained how
it works in great detail.

00:05:07.389 --> 00:05:12.010
So this scene was really exciting for book
readers and people that just watch the show.

00:05:12.010 --> 00:05:16.830
In fact, I’ll go on to say that I liked
this scene just as much as I liked Joffrey’s

00:05:16.830 --> 00:05:17.830
Death.

00:05:17.830 --> 00:05:20.500
And somehow, I have a feeling the show is
going to do something to top it before the

00:05:20.500 --> 00:05:21.500
season is over.

00:05:21.500 --> 00:05:28.380
But the big takeaway is that white walkers
aren’t born and they’re not undead like

00:05:28.380 --> 00:05:30.320
the wights.

00:05:30.320 --> 00:05:34.600
They’re turned as babies and raised.

00:05:34.600 --> 00:05:39.100
So much more we could talk about, but let
me know what your favorite WTF moment was.

00:05:39.100 --> 00:05:43.850
Court of the White Walkers, Burn Gorman just
being awesome or something else?

00:05:43.850 --> 00:05:50.370
Here’s a couple really important plot points
that we need to pay attention to but didn’t

00:05:50.370 --> 00:05:52.020
beat out my top 5 moments.

00:05:52.020 --> 00:05:56.389
Janos Slynt and Aliser Thorne were plotting
to get rid of Jon Snow by just letting him

00:05:56.389 --> 00:05:57.690
get himself killed at Crasters.

00:05:57.690 --> 00:05:59.690
Keep you eyes on them.

00:05:59.690 --> 00:06:03.570
Locke mysteriously appeared at the Night’s
Watch and seems like he’s tailing Jon Snow

00:06:03.570 --> 00:06:04.570
everywhere he goes.

00:06:04.570 --> 00:06:08.760
He’s just waiting for the right moment to
kill him for Roose Bolton to secure their

00:06:08.760 --> 00:06:10.220
claim on the North.

00:06:10.220 --> 00:06:14.190
The Kingslayer brothers are finally bonding
and I totally love it.

00:06:14.190 --> 00:06:20.750
The hatred they’re both getting from the
Cersei and Tywin is really bringing them together.

00:06:20.750 --> 00:06:25.322
It looks like the real reason the aged Tommen
up and recasted the actor was so that they

00:06:25.322 --> 00:06:27.990
could do these types of sexy Margaery scenes.

00:06:27.990 --> 00:06:32.310
How funny was it that the Queen of Thrones
revealed she killed Joffrey AND humped her

00:06:32.310 --> 00:06:36.990
husband so hard he couldn’t walk the night
before they got married.

00:06:36.990 --> 00:06:41.669
I used to think of her as being a female Tywin,
but she just got way more badass than Tywin.

00:06:41.669 --> 00:06:46.990
I was bummed they recast Tommen just for hump
day, but they totally gave us Ser Pounce,

00:06:46.990 --> 00:06:49.039
who was a really fun part of the books.

00:06:49.039 --> 00:06:52.949
So it’s like they take something away with
one hand and give us a treat with the other.

00:06:52.949 --> 00:06:57.919
And that reminds me, I heard at least three
separate characters make jokes about losing

00:06:57.919 --> 00:06:58.919
their right hand.

00:06:58.919 --> 00:07:00.820
It’s almost like the writers are trolling
Jaime.

00:07:00.820 --> 00:07:07.300
One of my favorite lines was when she said
“Marrying a Targaryen was all the rage back

00:07:07.300 --> 00:07:08.300
then.”

00:07:08.300 --> 00:07:13.490
Overall the episode was amazing, I gave it
a solid A for use of Burn Gorman and White

00:07:13.490 --> 00:07:14.569
Walkers.

00:07:14.569 --> 00:07:18.080
I think they did a good job of addressing
issues with Bran’s character from last season

00:07:18.080 --> 00:07:20.810
by bringing him back into the story around
the Wall.

00:07:20.810 --> 00:07:25.060
And I love that they’re making show Sansa
seem a lot smarter than book Sansa.

00:07:25.060 --> 00:07:29.330
So all in all, even though they did make some
big changes from the books.

00:07:29.330 --> 00:07:30.970
Namely the mega white walker scene.

00:07:30.970 --> 00:07:32.330
I totally love what they did.

00:07:32.330 --> 00:07:37.479
There were several really breathtaking scenes
that reminded me of last season when Jon Snow

00:07:37.479 --> 00:07:41.360
climbed the Wall and they showed the big wide
shot of the south side of the wall.

00:07:41.360 --> 00:07:43.380
Like Daenerys on top of the pyramid.

00:07:43.380 --> 00:07:47.009
There was also a really cool night shot of
the city when they were breaking in.

00:07:47.009 --> 00:07:51.419
And that Lord of the Rings white walker mountain.

00:07:51.419 --> 00:07:54.740
I think they’re able to spend money on that
kind of stuff because they don’t put dragons

00:07:54.740 --> 00:07:55.979
in every episode.

00:07:55.979 --> 00:07:59.090
So if you ever wondered why they aren’t
around all the time, it’s because they want

00:07:59.090 --> 00:08:01.220
to do big CG landscapes.

00:08:01.220 --> 00:08:04.860
Let me know if you have any other thoughts
about the big changes they made or the extra

00:08:04.860 --> 00:08:06.270
white walker scenes they included.

00:08:06.270 --> 00:08:07.720
And remember, my Q&amp;A will post tomorrow.

00:08:07.720 --> 00:08:09.940
So be sure to subscribe to get it.

00:08:09.940 --> 00:08:13.400
And leave me suggestions for future bonus
videos.

00:08:13.400 --> 00:08:17.980
Maybe a white walker one given what we just
saw.

00:08:17.980 --> 00:08:21.760
Right now click here for that Q&amp;A video, I’ll
add the annotation as soon as I post the video

00:08:21.760 --> 00:08:23.580
and click here to learn all about the Bloodraven.

00:08:23.580 --> 00:08:25.780
Thanks for watching, see you guys tomorrow.

00:08:25.780 --> 00:08:26.309
High Fives!

